      "farewell": "Wrote `answer_4213852742.preql` and validated it with `--run`.\n\nIt returns one row per policy (policy number, total premium paid):\n- 31003000336 \u2192 86,000\n- 31003000337 \u2192 12,000\n\nHow it works: the `Premium` model carries only the `policy_amount_identifier` key (no amount of its own), so the premium amounts are the `Policy_Amount.policy_amount` values for those premium keys. A membership semijoin (`where pa.policy_amount_identifier in pr.policy_amount_identifier`) restricts to premium rows, then `sum(pa.policy_amount)` groups automatically by the policy number reached through `Policy_Amount.Policy`.",
